IP increases along the period. But IP of Be > B. Further IP of O < N because atoms with fully or partly filled orbitals are most stable and hence have high ionisation energy. 

As in case of boron, 2p^1 electron have to be removed to get B^+(1s^2 2s^2) 
from B(1s^2 2s^2 2p^1), while in case of Be (1s^22s^2) electron have to be removed to get Be^+ (1s^22s^1). p electron can be removed more easily than s electron so the energy required to remove electron will be less in case of boron.

